A place has time while its virtual time lies up to two spans ahead of the clock, not one.
It would start requests its units have not paid for, before the threads on spare time;
a place has time while its request is open, or while its virtual time lies at most a span ahead of the clock.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a request started elsewhere than at the later of its virtual time and the clock, within a span of it
Witness: fuzz lend-own-time-comes

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -220,7 +220,7 @@ static uint32_t place_core(const struct place *p)
  */
 static bool has_time(const struct place *payer, const struct place *p, uint64_t now)
 {
-    return place_units(payer) != 0 && (request_open(payer, p) || payer->vt <= now + place_span(payer));
+    return place_units(payer) != 0 && (request_open(payer, p) || payer->vt <= now + 2 * (uint64_t)place_span(payer));
 }
 
 /* The count a place's units give it time again at, with no request open: its virtual time less its span. */
